body:
Just flagging that this first test might partially conflict with my suggestion to store the result in a static bool. If this is called sometimes while `get_singleton()` doesn't exist yet, but it's created later, that check should likely happen before the static bool, so:
```cpp
if (!get_singleton()) {
	return false;
}

static bool rd_creation_tested = false;
static bool can_create_rd = false;

if (!rd_creation_tested) {
	// all further checks}
}

return can_create_rd;
```

